  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY NIGHT THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 1231 AM MDT Mon Aug 24 2026\n\nExpect a slightly stronger westward push of moisture Tue night\ninto Wed behind departing central plains convection, with deeper\nmoisture and instability along and east of the mountains during\nthe day, though potential for early morning stratus could hamper\ninstability initially. Overall, expect Wed to be perhaps the\nmost convectively active day of the week, with heavy rain threat\nover much of the region and at least a low end severe threat\nalong and east of I-25. Cooler temps expected Wed with clouds\nand moisture, and maxes will end up near/below seasonal \naverages for a change at many locations. \n\nUpper ridge drifts west and expands northward for the end of the\nweek, before potentially flattening and drifting back eastward \nearly next week. Overall, expect a slow drying/warming trend \nfrom Thu into the weekend, though enough recycled moisture will\nbe around for daily afternoon and evening thunderstorms, \nespecially over the mountains. Plains could see still see some \nstorms Thu/Fri, before most activity retreats into the higher \nterrain over the weekend. Max temps will drift upward through \nthe period, with 80s/90s widespread and even a few 100 degf \nreadings returning to the plains.",
